{"name":"Mountain Lake","hex":"#2d5975","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mountain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An elevation of land of considerable dimensions rising more or less abruptly, forming a conspicuous figure in the landscape, usually having a small extent of surface at its summit. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Something very large in size or quantity; a huge amount; a great heap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mountain"},{"term":"lake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, landlocked stretch of water or similar liquid.","A large amount of liquid."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An offering, sacrifice, gift.","Play; sport; game; fun; glee."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mountain Lake (Ontario)","blocks":[{"text":"Mountain Lake (Ontario) may refer to one of a number of lakes in Ontario, Canada with this precise name or to others with similar names."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain_Lake_(Ontario)","wikidata":"Q6925036"},{"title":"Mountain Lake (Virginia)","blocks":[{"text":"Mountain Lake is a freshwater lake located in Giles County near Newport, Virginia in the United States. Along with Lake Drummond in the Great Dismal Swamp, it is one of only two natural lakes in Virginia. It was originally known as Salt Pond, as it was where cattle were given salt."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Mountain_Lake_Virginia_lakeview.jpg/330px-Mountain_Lake_Virginia_lakeview.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain_Lake_(Virginia)","wikidata":"Q1950851"},{"title":"Mountain","blocks":[{"text":"A mountain is an elevated portion of the surface of a planet, generally with steep sides that show significant exposed bedrock. Although there are no universally accepted definitions, a mountain is usually considered higher than a hill. By definition, mountains are often thought of as being a landform which is higher than 2,000 feet (610 m). It may either have a limited summit area or be a smaller plateau with high elevation and steep sides. A few mountains are isolated summits, but most occur in mountain ranges."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Everest_North_Face_toward_Base_Camp_Tibet_Luca_Galuzzi_2006.jpg/330px-Everest_North_Face_toward_Base_Camp_Tibet_Luca_Galuzzi_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain","wikidata":"Q8502"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Mountain_Lake_Virginia_lakeview.jpg/500px-Mountain_Lake_Virginia_lakeview.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Mountain_Lake_Virginia_lakeview.jpg/1280px-Mountain_Lake_Virginia_lakeview.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Mountain_Lake_Virginia_lakeview.jpg/500px-Mountain_Lake_Virginia_lakeview.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMountain_Lake_Virginia_lakeview.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Mountain_Lake_Virginia_Hotel.jpg/500px-Mountain_Lake_Virginia_Hotel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Mountain_Lake_Virginia_Hotel.jpg/1280px-Mountain_Lake_Virginia_Hotel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Mountain_Lake_Virginia_Hotel.jpg/500px-Mountain_Lake_Virginia_Hotel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conte